#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:6
msgid "Skill Creator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:8
msgid "This skill provides guidance for creating effective skills."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:10
msgid "About Skills"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:12
msgid ""
"Skills are modular, self-contained packages that extend the agent's "
"capabilities by providing specialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. "
"Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific domains or tasks—they"
" transform the agent from a general-purpose agent into a specialized "
"agent equipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:17
msgid "What Skills Provide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:19
msgid "Specialized workflows - Multi-step procedures for specific domains"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:20
msgid ""
"Tool integrations - Instructions for working with specific file formats "
"or APIs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:21
msgid "Domain expertise - Company-specific knowledge, schemas, business logic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:22
msgid ""
"Bundled resources - Scripts, references, and assets for complex and "
"repetitive tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:24
msgid "Core Principles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:26
msgid "Concise is Key"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:28
msgid ""
"The context window is a public good. Skills share the context window with"
" everything else the agent needs: system prompt, conversation history, "
"other Skills' metadata, and the actual user request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:30
msgid ""
"**Default assumption: the agent is already very smart.** Only add context"
" the agent doesn't already have. Challenge each piece of information: "
"\"Does the agent really need this explanation?\" and \"Does this "
"paragraph justify its token cost?\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:32
msgid "Prefer concise examples over verbose explanations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:34
msgid "Set Appropriate Degrees of Freedom"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:36
msgid "Match the level of specificity to the task's fragility and variability:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:38
msgid ""
"**High freedom (text-based instructions)**: Use when multiple approaches "
"are valid, decisions depend on context, or heuristics guide the approach."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:40
msgid ""
"**Medium freedom (pseudocode or scripts with parameters)**: Use when a "
"preferred pattern exists, some variation is acceptable, or configuration "
"affects behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:42
msgid ""
"**Low freedom (specific scripts, few parameters)**: Use when operations "
"are fragile and error-prone, consistency is critical, or a specific "
"sequence must be followed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:44
msgid ""
"Think of the agent as exploring a path: a narrow bridge with cliffs needs"
" specific guardrails (low freedom), while an open field allows many "
"routes (high freedom)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:46
msgid "Anatomy of a Skill"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:48
msgid ""
"Every skill consists of a required SKILL.md file and optional bundled "
"resources:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:63
msgid "SKILL.md (required)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:65
msgid "Every SKILL.md consists of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:67
msgid ""
"**Frontmatter** (YAML): Contains `name` and `description` fields. These "
"are the only fields that the agent reads to determine when the skill gets"
" used, thus it is very important to be clear and comprehensive in "
"describing what the skill is, and when it should be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:68
msgid ""
"**Body** (Markdown): Instructions and guidance for using the skill. Only "
"loaded AFTER the skill triggers (if at all)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:70
msgid "Bundled Resources (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:72
msgid "Scripts (`scripts/`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:74
msgid ""
"Executable code (Python/Bash/etc.) for tasks that require deterministic "
"reliability or are repeatedly rewritten."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:76
msgid ""
"**When to include**: When the same code is being rewritten repeatedly or "
"deterministic reliability is needed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:77
msgid "**Example**: `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` for PDF rotation tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:78
msgid ""
"**Benefits**: Token efficient, deterministic, may be executed without "
"loading into context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:79
msgid ""
"**Note**: Scripts may still need to be read by the agent for patching or "
"environment-specific adjustments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:81
msgid "References (`references/`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:83
msgid ""
"Documentation and reference material intended to be loaded as needed into"
" context to inform the agent's process and thinking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:85
msgid ""
"**When to include**: For documentation that the agent should reference "
"while working"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:86
msgid ""
"**Examples**: `references/finance.md` for financial schemas, "
"`references/mnda.md` for company NDA template, `references/policies.md` "
"for company policies, `references/api_docs.md` for API specifications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:87
msgid ""
"**Use cases**: Database schemas, API documentation, domain knowledge, "
"company policies, detailed workflow guides"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:88
msgid ""
"**Benefits**: Keeps SKILL.md lean, loaded only when the agent determines "
"it's needed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:89
msgid ""
"**Best practice**: If files are large (>10k words), include grep search "
"patterns in SKILL.md"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:90
msgid ""
"**Avoid duplication**: Information should live in either SKILL.md or "
"references files, not both. Prefer references files for detailed "
"information unless it's truly core to the skill—this keeps SKILL.md lean "
"while making information discoverable without hogging the context window."
" Keep only essential procedural instructions and workflow guidance in "
"SKILL.md; move detailed reference material, schemas, and examples to "
"references files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:92
msgid "Assets (`assets/`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:94
msgid ""
"Files not intended to be loaded into context, but rather used within the "
"output the agent produces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:96
msgid ""
"**When to include**: When the skill needs files that will be used in the "
"final output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:97
msgid ""
"**Examples**: `assets/logo.png` for brand assets, `assets/slides.pptx` "
"for PowerPoint templates, `assets/frontend-template/` for HTML/React "
"boilerplate, `assets/font.ttf` for typography"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:98
msgid ""
"**Use cases**: Templates, images, icons, boilerplate code, fonts, sample "
"documents that get copied or modified"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:99
msgid ""
"**Benefits**: Separates output resources from documentation, enables the "
"agent to use files without loading them into context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:101
msgid "What to Not Include in a Skill"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:103
msgid ""
"A skill should only contain essential files that directly support its "
"functionality. Do NOT create extraneous documentation or auxiliary files,"
" including:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:105
msgid "README.md"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:106
msgid "INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:107
msgid "QUICK_REFERENCE.md"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:108
msgid "CHANGELOG.md"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:109
msgid "etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:111
msgid ""
"The skill should only contain the information needed for an AI agent to "
"do the job at hand. It should not contain auxiliary context about the "
"process that went into creating it, setup and testing procedures, user-"
"facing documentation, etc. Creating additional documentation files just "
"adds clutter and confusion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:113
msgid "Progressive Disclosure Design Principle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:115
msgid "Skills use a three-level loading system to manage context efficiently:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:117
msgid "**Metadata (name + description)** - Always in context (~100 words)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:118
msgid "**SKILL.md body** - When skill triggers (<5k words)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:119
msgid ""
"**Bundled resources** - As needed by the agent (Unlimited because scripts"
" can be executed without reading into context window)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:121
msgid "Progressive Disclosure Patterns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:123
msgid ""
"Keep SKILL.md body to the essentials and under 500 lines to minimize "
"context bloat. Split content into separate files when approaching this "
"limit. When splitting out content into other files, it is very important "
"to reference them from SKILL.md and describe clearly when to read them, "
"to ensure the reader of the skill knows they exist and when to use them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:125
msgid ""
"**Key principle:** When a skill supports multiple variations, frameworks,"
" or options, keep only the core workflow and selection guidance in "
"SKILL.md. Move variant-specific details (patterns, examples, "
"configuration) into separate reference files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:127
msgid "**Pattern 1: High-level guide with references**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:144
msgid "the agent loads FORMS.md, REFERENCE.md, or EXAMPLES.md only when needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:146
msgid "**Pattern 2: Domain-specific organization**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:148
msgid ""
"For Skills with multiple domains, organize content by domain to avoid "
"loading irrelevant context:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:160
msgid "When a user asks about sales metrics, the agent only reads sales.md."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:162
msgid ""
"Similarly, for skills supporting multiple frameworks or variants, "
"organize by variant:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:173
msgid "When the user chooses AWS, the agent only reads aws.md."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:175
msgid "**Pattern 3: Conditional details**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:177
msgid "Show basic content, link to advanced content:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:194
msgid ""
"the agent reads REDLINING.md or OOXML.md only when the user needs those "
"features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:196
msgid "**Important guidelines:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:198
msgid ""
"**Avoid deeply nested references** - Keep references one level deep from "
"SKILL.md. All reference files should link directly from SKILL.md."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:199
msgid ""
"**Structure longer reference files** - For files longer than 100 lines, "
"include a table of contents at the top so the agent can see the full "
"scope when previewing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:201
msgid "Skill Creation Process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:203
msgid "Skill creation involves these steps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:205
msgid "Understand the skill with concrete examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:206
msgid "Plan reusable skill contents (scripts, references, assets)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:207
msgid "Initialize the skill (run init_skill.py)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:208
msgid "Edit the skill (implement resources and write SKILL.md)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:209
msgid "Package the skill (run package_skill.py)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:210
msgid "Iterate based on real usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:212
msgid ""
"Follow these steps in order, skipping only if there is a clear reason why"
" they are not applicable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:214
msgid "Skill Naming"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:216
msgid ""
"Use lowercase letters, digits, and hyphens only; normalize user-provided "
"titles to hyphen-case (e.g., \"Plan Mode\" -> `plan-mode`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:217
msgid ""
"When generating names, generate a name under 64 characters (letters, "
"digits, hyphens)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:218
msgid "Prefer short, verb-led phrases that describe the action."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:219
msgid ""
"Namespace by tool when it improves clarity or triggering (e.g., `gh-"
"address-comments`, `linear-address-issue`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:220
msgid "Name the skill folder exactly after the skill name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:222
msgid "Step 1: Understanding the Skill with Concrete Examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:224
msgid ""
"Skip this step only when the skill's usage patterns are already clearly "
"understood. It remains valuable even when working with an existing skill."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:226
msgid ""
"To create an effective skill, clearly understand concrete examples of how"
" the skill will be used. This understanding can come from either direct "
"user examples or generated examples that are validated with user "
"feedback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:228
msgid ""
"For example, when building an image-editor skill, relevant questions "
"include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:230
msgid ""
"\"What functionality should the image-editor skill support? Editing, "
"rotating, anything else?\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:231
msgid "\"Can you give some examples of how this skill would be used?\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:232
msgid ""
"\"I can imagine users asking for things like 'Remove the red-eye from "
"this image' or 'Rotate this image'. Are there other ways you imagine this"
" skill being used?\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:233
msgid "\"What would a user say that should trigger this skill?\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:235
msgid ""
"To avoid overwhelming users, avoid asking too many questions in a single "
"message. Start with the most important questions and follow up as needed "
"for better effectiveness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:237
msgid ""
"Conclude this step when there is a clear sense of the functionality the "
"skill should support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:239
msgid "Step 2: Planning the Reusable Skill Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:241
msgid ""
"To turn concrete examples into an effective skill, analyze each example "
"by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:243
msgid "Considering how to execute on the example from scratch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:244
msgid ""
"Identifying what scripts, references, and assets would be helpful when "
"executing these workflows repeatedly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:246
msgid ""
"Example: When building a `pdf-editor` skill to handle queries like \"Help"
" me rotate this PDF,\" the analysis shows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:248
msgid "Rotating a PDF requires re-writing the same code each time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:249
msgid "A `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` script would be helpful to store in the skill"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:251
msgid ""
"Example: When designing a `frontend-webapp-builder` skill for queries "
"like \"Build me a todo app\" or \"Build me a dashboard to track my "
"steps,\" the analysis shows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:253
msgid ""
"Writing a frontend webapp requires the same boilerplate HTML/React each "
"time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:254
msgid ""
"An `assets/hello-world/` template containing the boilerplate HTML/React "
"project files would be helpful to store in the skill"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:256
msgid ""
"Example: When building a `big-query` skill to handle queries like \"How "
"many users have logged in today?\" the analysis shows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:258
msgid ""
"Querying BigQuery requires re-discovering the table schemas and "
"relationships each time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:259
msgid ""
"A `references/schema.md` file documenting the table schemas would be "
"helpful to store in the skill"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:261
msgid ""
"To establish the skill's contents, analyze each concrete example to "
"create a list of the reusable resources to include: scripts, references, "
"and assets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:263
msgid "Step 3: Initializing the Skill"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:265
msgid "At this point, it is time to actually create the skill."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:267
msgid ""
"Skip this step only if the skill being developed already exists, and "
"iteration or packaging is needed. In this case, continue to the next "
"step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:269
msgid ""
"When creating a new skill from scratch, always run the `init_skill.py` "
"script. The script conveniently generates a new template skill directory "
"that automatically includes everything a skill requires, making the skill"
" creation process much more efficient and reliable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:271
msgid "Usage:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:277
msgid "Examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:285
msgid "The script:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:287
msgid "Creates the skill directory at the specified path"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:288
msgid ""
"Generates a SKILL.md template with proper frontmatter and TODO "
"placeholders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:289
msgid "Optionally creates resource directories based on `--resources`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:290
msgid "Optionally adds example files when `--examples` is set"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:292
msgid ""
"After initialization, customize the SKILL.md and add resources as needed."
" If you used `--examples`, replace or delete placeholder files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:294
msgid "Step 4: Edit the Skill"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:296
msgid ""
"When editing the (newly-generated or existing) skill, remember that the "
"skill is being created for another instance of the agent to use. Include "
"information that would be beneficial and non-obvious to the agent. "
"Consider what procedural knowledge, domain-specific details, or reusable "
"assets would help another the agent instance execute these tasks more "
"effectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:298
msgid "Learn Proven Design Patterns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:300
msgid "Consult these helpful guides based on your skill's needs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:302
msgid ""
"**Multi-step processes**: See references/workflows.md for sequential "
"workflows and conditional logic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:303
msgid ""
"**Specific output formats or quality standards**: See references/output-"
"patterns.md for template and example patterns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:305
msgid "These files contain established best practices for effective skill design."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:307
msgid "Start with Reusable Skill Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:309
msgid ""
"To begin implementation, start with the reusable resources identified "
"above: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` files. Note that this "
"step may require user input. For example, when implementing a `brand-"
"guidelines` skill, the user may need to provide brand assets or templates"
" to store in `assets/`, or documentation to store in `references/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:311
msgid ""
"Added scripts must be tested by actually running them to ensure there are"
" no bugs and that the output matches what is expected. If there are many "
"similar scripts, only a representative sample needs to be tested to "
"ensure confidence that they all work while balancing time to completion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:313
msgid ""
"If you used `--examples`, delete any placeholder files that are not "
"needed for the skill. Only create resource directories that are actually "
"required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:315
msgid "Update SKILL.md"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:317
msgid "**Writing Guidelines:** Always use imperative/infinitive form."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:319
msgid "Frontmatter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:321
msgid "Write the YAML frontmatter with `name` and `description`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:323
msgid "`name`: The skill name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:324
msgid ""
"`description`: This is the primary triggering mechanism for your skill, "
"and helps the agent understand when to use the skill."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:325
msgid ""
"Include both what the Skill does and specific triggers/contexts for when "
"to use it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:326
msgid ""
"Include all \"when to use\" information here - Not in the body. The body "
"is only loaded after triggering, so \"When to Use This Skill\" sections "
"in the body are not helpful to the agent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:327
msgid ""
"Example description for a `docx` skill: \"Comprehensive document "
"creation, editing, and analysis with support for tracked changes, "
"comments, formatting preservation, and text extraction. Use when the "
"agent needs to work with professional documents (.docx files) for: (1) "
"Creating new documents, (2) Modifying or editing content, (3) Working "
"with tracked changes, (4) Adding comments, or any other document tasks\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:329
msgid "Do not include any other fields in YAML frontmatter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:331
msgid "Body"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:333
msgid "Write instructions for using the skill and its bundled resources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:335
msgid "Step 5: Packaging a Skill"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:337
msgid ""
"Once development of the skill is complete, it must be packaged into a "
"distributable .skill file that gets shared with the user. The packaging "
"process automatically validates the skill first to ensure it meets all "
"requirements:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/skill-creator_SKILL.md:343
